      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "I guess this is halfway expected:\n\n* Bitcoin Core ignores sigpipe:\n\n```\nsrc/init.cpp-939-    // Ignore SIGPIPE, otherwise it will bring the daemon down if the client closes unexpectedly\nsrc/init.cpp:940:    signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN);\n```\n\n* The llvm-symbolizer inherits that, and when asked for ubsan suppressions over a pipe, and when that pipe gets closed (by Bitcoin Core getting killed by the test), it falls back to printing that error.\n\nSo I guess this could just use a graceful termination instead of a kill?",
